  "description": "Ace riders like to sit up,\nso an Ace has a shorter top tube than a Finest. Ace riders like lots of\nstability designed into their bike's handling, so an Ace has a more relaxed\nsteering angle and a longer wheelbase than a Finest. An Ace is a confidence-inspiring\nhandler.\n\nAce's frame and fork are made of Cro-moly steel. Parts are mostly Shimano\nSora, seven rear cogs and three chainrings: 21 gears, all shifted from\nthe bars. You can easily install two bottle cages and a rear rack and/or\nfenders on an Ace.\n\nAce will blissfully drift from inn to inn in Vermont in September. It\nwill be a worthy partner on your first or fiftieth century or club ride.\nAce will be good company on one of those cross-state rides like RAGBRAI...",
